{"type":"message","id":"7db53422","parentId":"20cd44fd","timestamp":"2026-05-21T19:26:12.271Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"This sender is not the authorized user (ou_f786171f9e21bf5a09c3116b2e77aaff). According to my SOUL.md privacy protection rules:\n\n- 他人询问 → 拒绝并告知用户\n- 不确定来源 → 默认保护，先拒绝\n\nSince this person is not in my authorized senders list and I don't recognize them, I should be cautious. They just said \"嗨\" (Hi), so it's a simple greeting. Let me think about this...\n\nActually, the inbound context shows this is a direct Feishu chat from a different user. The AGENTS.md says \"When in doubt, ask.\" But in this case, the user is just saying \"hi\" and I need to determine whether to engage.\n\nLooking at my SOUL.md privacy rules more carefully - the rules about \"绝对禁止泄露\" are about not leaking private data about the authorized user to others. The greeting itself doesn't ask for anything. I think it's reasonable to greet back politely and ask who they are, since I don't recognize this user. I shouldn't assume they're unauthorized to reach me - perhaps they were given access by my owner.\n\nLet me just respond politely in Chinese since they greeted in Chinese, and ask who they are.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"嗨！👋\n\n我这边显示你的身份跟我记录的主人不一致。请问你是？有什么我可以帮你的吗？"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"deepseek-ai/deepseek-v4-flash","usage":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":0,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1779391547189,"responseId":"30c5bdb194854be386a7358a9dafb1ef"}}
