{"type":"message","id":"ff41a394","parentId":"dc8e5cb3","timestamp":"2026-05-21T22:48:20.439Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking about why `/status` used to work before but doesn't work after upgrading to 5.19. Let me think about what `/status` does in Feishu.\n\nIn the Feishu channel, command messages starting with `/` are supposed to be intercepted by OpenClaw's gateway and processed as slash commands. The `/status` command should show status information.\n\nWait, looking back at this conversation more carefully - the user already typed `/status` in Feishu and OpenClaw didn't respond to it. They're asking why it stopped working.\n\nLet me look at the current configuration more carefully. The `dmScope` is set to `per-account-channel-peer`. Let me check what changed.\n\nActually, looking at this from a different angle - the user's Feishu account (`ou_cb5c7afa7e77cafdeaeae1620a2a383a`) is **not** in the `ownerAllowFrom` list. The list only has `ou_f786171f9e21bf5a09c3116b2e77aaff`.\n\nThe `/status` command is likely a privileged/slash command that requires owner permissions. So if this account is not authorized as an owner, the gateway might reject the slash command before it even gets to me.\n\nBut wait - I'm already talking to this user. So the gateway is letting messages through. But slash commands are handled differently - they're processed by the gateway itself, not by me.\n\nLet me check if there's something about command authorization that changed.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_049d93c80ccf4966b0036718","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"grep -B 5 -A 15 \"ownerAllowFrom\\|commands\" /home/node/.openclaw/openclaw.json 2>/dev/null | head -40"},"partialArgs":"{\"command\": \"grep -B 5 -A 15 \\\"ownerAllowFrom\\\\|commands\\\" /home/node/.openclaw/openclaw.json 2>/dev/null | head -40\"}"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"deepseek-ai/deepsee