{"type":"message","id":"4667783b","parentId":"479536a3","timestamp":"2026-05-22T01:20:49.554Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user says `/status` used to work before, but now it doesn't. They mention \"ssh\" at the end, which might be a typo or they're referring to something else. Let me think about this.\n\nThe timing is interesting - the system says context was compacted at 2026-05-21 23:11 UTC. The current message is at 2026-05-22 01:19 UTC.\n\nThe user seems frustrated. They're saying `/status` worked before but now it doesn't since upgrading. Let me check if there's a discrepancy between the authorized ID and their current ID that could have happened during an upgrade.\n\nActually, looking at this more carefully - the user said \"之前都能用啊\" (it used to work) and then added \"ssh\" which might be a typo for \"啊\" or could be referencing something else.\n\nLet me reconsider. The user's current Feishu ID is `ou_cb5c7afa7e77cafdeaeae1620a2a383a`, but the config has `ou_f786171f9e21bf5a09c3116b2e77aaff`. \n\nBut wait - the key insight here might be about `dmScope: \"per-account-channel-peer\"`. With this setting, each Feishu account gets its own DM session. The `/status` command should still work within a DM even if the user isn't in `ownerAllowFrom` - unless there's a difference between \"owner commands\" and regular slash commands.\n\nActually, let me re-read the pairing docs. In the pairing doc it says:\n\"commands.ownerAllowFrom: the approved sender, such as telegram:123456789\"\n\"If no command owner is configured yet, approving a DM pairing code also bootstraps commands.ownerAllowFrom to the approved sender\"\n\nSo `ownerAllowFrom` controls who can use privileged/owner-level commands. `/status` might be an owner-only command.\n\nBut the user says it used to work. So what changed? The upgrade to 2026.5.19.\n\nLet me check if there's something in the changelog about this, or if the `commands` block could have been changed during upgrade.\n\nActually, thinking about it more - the user might be right that it worked before. The question is why. Some possibilities:\n\n1. The config was changed/overwritten during the upgrade process\n2. The previous version didn't enforce `ownerAllowFrom` for all commands like `/status`\n3. They were using a different account before\n\nI don't have the git log access to see the changelog. Let me take a more practical approach and focus on helping the user fix this.\n\nActually, I realize I should just be straightforward with the user. They're saying it worked before, I should take them at their word and figure out what changed.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"你说得对，让我再挖一下，看升级到 "},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_e4e3406c39c54329959b490b","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# Check if there's a changelog or release notes\nfind /app -name \"CHANGELOG*\" -o -name \"RELEASE*\" -o -name \"HISTORY*\" 2>/dev/null | head -5"},"partialArgs":"{\"command\": \"# Check if there's a changelog or release notes\\nfind /app -name \\\"CHANGELOG*\\\" -o -name \\\"RELEASE*\\\" -o -name \\\"HISTORY*\\\" 2>/dev/null | head -5\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_2270830d5f5248feb1cedb25","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# Check if commands block was recently added or modified in config\nstat /home/node/.openclaw/openclaw.json 2>/dev/null\necho \"---\"\n# Check if there's a backup of the config\nls -la /home/node/.openclaw/openclaw.json.bak* 2>/dev/null || echo \"no backup found\""},"partialArgs":"{\"command\": \"# Check if commands block was recently added or modified in config\\nstat /home/node/.openclaw/openclaw.json 2>/dev/null\\necho \\\"---\\\"\\n# Check if there's a backup of the config\\nls -la /home/node/.openclaw/openclaw.json.bak* 2>/dev/null || echo \\\"no backup found\\\"\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_619705c3a2b543069f93c2ba","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# Check if there are any other config files or overrides\nfi