{"type":"message","id":"ff61b161","parentId":"cfdc7edd","timestamp":"2026-05-22T01:24:41.566Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The config was modified at 23:09 UTC, and the gateway has been up for 17h 40m according to the session_status output earlier. But the uptime was from the session_status tool, not /proc/uptime. Let me check if the gateway needs a restart for the config change to take effect.\n\nActually, looking at the session_status output more carefully: \"⏱️ Uptime: gateway 17h 40m\" - so the gateway started around 17h40m before 2026-05-22 01:19 UTC, which would be around 2026-05-21 07:39 UTC.\n\nThe config was modified at 2026-05-21 23:09 UTC. So the gateway was already running when the config was updated. The gateway may need a restart to pick up the config change.\n\nBut wait - the user is currently talking to me through the gateway. The gateway is clearly running. Since the config was updated at 23:09 but gateway started at ~07:39, the config change may not have been picked up yet unless OpenClaw watches for config file changes.\n\nLet me check if `/status` would work now. Actually, the user just sent a normal message, not `/status`. Let me check if the gateway has been restarted since the config change.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"配置文件在 23:09 UTC（大约15分钟前）才被修改的，但网关已经跑了 17 个小时没重启过。所以这个加了你 ID 的配置可能**还没生效**。\n\n要不要我帮你重启一下网关，让配置生效？这样 `/status` 应该就能用了。"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"deepseek-ai/deepseek-v4-flash","usage":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":0,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1779413057995,"responseId":"6f6abfe6337547bb90b018095f7b7838"}}
